## 🔌 Phase 3: Connecting to Existing Approval Logic

In your existing `app/Http/Controllers/Api/MaintenanceTicketController.php`, locate the `approve()` method (lines 336–366) and dispatch the job right after the ticket status is updated:

### Modified `approve()` Method in `MaintenanceTicketController.php`:

```php
    /**
     * Approve a maintenance ticket (Admin only).
     */
    public function approve(Request $request, $id)
    {
        Gate::authorize('manage', MaintenanceTicket::class);

        $ticket = MaintenanceTicket::findOrFail($id);

        if ($ticket->status !== 'submitted') {
            return response()->json(['message' => 'Ticket cannot be approved in current status'], 400);
        }

        $ticket->update([
            'status' => 'approved',
            'approved_by' => auth()->user()->profile->id,
            'approved_at' => now(),
        ]);

        ActivityLogger::log('approved', 'Ticket', $ticket->id, "Approved ticket: {$ticket->title}");

        // 1. In-App Notification to Requester
        if ($ticket->requester && $ticket->requester->user_id) {
            $this->createNotification(
                $ticket->requester->user_id,
                'Ticket Approved',
                "Your ticket '{$ticket->title}' has been approved.",
                'success',
                "/tickets/{$ticket->id}"
            );
        }

        // 2. DISPATCH MICROSOFT GRAPH API EMAIL NOTIFICATION JOB
        \App\Jobs\SendTicketApprovalNotification::dispatch($ticket);

        return response()->json($ticket->load('approvedBy', 'requester'));
    }
```

---

## ✅ Phase 4: Verification & Logging

1. **Test in Local / Staging:**
   Run the Laravel queue worker to process jobs:
   ```bash
   php artisan queue:work
   ```
2. **Approve a Ticket:**
   Approve any submitted ticket through the Admin Dashboard interface or API endpoint `/api/tickets/{id}/approve`.
3. **Verify Logs:**
   Check `storage/logs/laravel.log`:
   ```
   [2026-08-09 21:25:00] local.INFO: Ticket approval notification email successfully sent via Graph API to user@eeigconstruction.com for Ticket #...
   ```
4. **Verify Recipient Inbox:**
   The recipient receives the formatted HTML email sent from `system@eeigconstruction.com` via Exchange Online.
